# The entrypoint is run by /bin/sh inside a Linux container, and the image is
# built from the working tree. On Windows, where core.autocrlf=true, a CRLF
# checkout makes the shebang line read `/bin/sh<CR>` - and the container then
# fails to start with a "no such file or directory" naming a file that plainly
# exists, which is a genuinely baffling half hour. Pin it.
*.sh text eol=lf
